00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.100
And as we've been
talking to customers

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.940
over and over and over again,
we hear three main concerns

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.300
every single time.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.230
The first one is, people
have trouble managing

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.662
infrastructure.

00:01:08.662 --> 00:01:10.620
Whenever you're talking
about machine learning,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.170
you've got GPUs TPUs, CPUs.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.282
You have to do
distributed training.

00:01:15.282 --> 00:01:16.740
It's kind of a
nightmare sometimes,

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.060
and some people would
rather not do it.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.030
Some people just can't.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.950
In addition, the
real world is hybrid.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.910
There's stuff on Cloud,
there's stuff on prem.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.810
Anytime you have one
of those boundaries,

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:30.810
it gets to be a little
bit of a nightmare trying

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.220
to move workloads
from one to the other.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.460
That's a problem that
we want to solve.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.160
The second problem we hear is
really about a talent problem.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.740
There's just not enough
talent to go around.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.270
You've got a data
scientist, you've

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:43.650
got production
engineers that are

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.800
used to putting those machine
learning jobs into production.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.800
There's just not enough.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.030
So we need to figure out
how to create 10 times force

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.790
multipliers for those teams,
so they can do 10 times

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:59.790
more projects and really enable
and empower your organizations.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:02.040
To do that, we need
collaboration tools that

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:05.940
actually focus on reuse and
collaboration across teams,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.370
and essentially create
a center of excellence

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.900
within your organizations
to meet your needs.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.275
That's the theme you're going
to hear over and over again

00:02:13.275 --> 00:02:13.890
in this talk.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:17.070
The third problem that we keep
hearing is, people are having

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.110
a tough time getting started.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.000
And the reason is
because machine learning

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.210
is a very large
area of learning,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.770
and so some people
are new to cloud.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:29.700
Some people are new
to machine learning.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.900
Some people are new to specific
techniques within machine

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.690
learning or to putting
those jobs into production.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.700
Each one of those has a
different learning front

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.590
and so the question
is, how do each of us

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:43.150
gets started more quickly?

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.000
So how does Cloud AI help?

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.710
We have a number of new
products we're launching today,

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:51.130
including the AI Hub, along
with our new managed notebooks,

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:54.630
and we're going to demo
a number of these today,

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:58.080
as well as our Kubeflow Fairing
system, which we'll also

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.150
demo as well.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.810
Really quickly, one of
the things to remember

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.460
is AI is really a team sport.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.430
If you've ever seen
an organization put

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.600
a machine learning
model into production,

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:14.640
it usually takes a database
expert, the actual subject

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.753
matter expert, the
data scientist,

00:03:16.753 --> 00:03:18.420
somebody from the
production engineering

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.688
teams to actually get
this to all work together.

00:03:20.688 --> 00:03:23.230
So you really need to make sure
they're all working together.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:26.250
So if we think about
this, each person

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.470
has a role to do in a company.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.770
That role or that person might
have a different skill set.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:35.260
They need different tools
to be able to do their job.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.430
So the question is, how do we
make each one of these roles,

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.110
each one of these
people, successful

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.580
using machine
learning in the way

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.862
that they need to,
to do their job?

00:03:44.862 --> 00:03:46.570
So really quickly, to
