00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:45.080
Now, one of the
critical problems

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.360
we hear about over and over
again is about a lack of data.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:51.140
So if you're trying to do an
image classification model,

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.660
for instance, you may not
have millions of images,

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.750
but you might have
100 or 200 or 1,000

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.180
for your particular problem.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:12:59.930
Well, how do you
solve this problem?

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:01.820
The technique of
transfer learning

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:05.330
is a way that you can use
an open source pre trained

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:08.630
model, that has been trained
on a general data set,

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:11.030
to learn the general features.

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:13.460
And then you can then
switch over to your data set

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:19.580
and fine tune it on your
data to really quickly train

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:21.147
on your problem.

00:13:21.147 --> 00:13:22.730
And so we have a
number of these here,

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:25.910
and so you can see in the Hub--

