is that TFMA is also available
through Kubeflow Pipelines.

00:41:08.850 --> 00:41:10.440
And so what is TFMA?

00:41:10.440 --> 00:41:13.470
So TFMA is a part of TFX.

00:41:13.470 --> 00:41:16.210
it stands for TensorFlow
Model Analysis.

00:41:16.210 --> 00:41:17.340
So let's break that open.

00:41:17.340 --> 00:41:20.070
So, again, Kubeflow
Pipelines is a rich UI

00:41:20.070 --> 00:41:24.960
and it lets you pop out
to the TFMA Visualization.

00:41:24.960 --> 00:41:29.400
So TFMA let you view
your model's performance

00:41:29.400 --> 00:41:31.870
at different cross
sections of your data.

00:41:31.870 --> 00:41:34.560
So then you can pinpoint
where your model is not

00:41:34.560 --> 00:41:35.800
performing very well.

00:41:35.800 --> 00:41:38.040
And then you can iterate
and improve that model.

00:41:38.040 --> 00:41:39.930
This is extremely
powerful as you're

00:41:39.930 --> 00:41:43.652
trying to find the best
model for your use case.

00:41:43.652 --> 00:41:46.110
So here, we can kind of see
everything it gives back to us.

00:41:46.110 --> 00:41:49.500
The trip start hours
was split up by time,

00:41:49.500 --> 00:41:51.360
and we can see how
well it performed

00:41:51.360 --> 00:41:54.580
at each hour of the day.

00:41:54.580 --> 00:41:56.320
So let's close that.

00:41:56.320 --> 00:41:58.430
There are a few more
features down at the bottom.

00:41:58.430 --> 00:42:00.490
